"@type":"City","name":"Brattleboro","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Vermont"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Bennington","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Vermont"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Middlebury","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Vermont"}},{"@type":"City","name":"St. Johnsbury","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Vermont"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Stowe","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Vermont"}},{"@type":"City","name":"Hartford","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Vermont"}}],"knowsAbout":["Insurance appraisal","Appraisal clause","Property claim valuation","Ice dam claims","Snow load collapse","Flood and water damage claims"],"openingHoursSpecification":[{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00"}]},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/#website","url":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/","name":"Vermont Insurance Appraiser","publisher":{"@id":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/#webpage","url":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/","name":"Vermont Insurance Appraisal Process | 8 Clear Steps","description":"The Vermont insurance appraisal process in eight steps: the written demand, naming appraisers, choosing an umpire and the binding award.","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"dateModified":"2026-11-17","primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/timber-frame.webp","width":1200,"height":900},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/#breadcrumb"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/#howto"}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Appraisal process","item":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/"}],"@id":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"HowTo","name":"How the insurance appraisal process works in Vermont","description":"The steps of a property insurance appraisal under a typical appraisal clause.","step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"Pin down the disagreement","text":"Appraisal is for one kind of dispute: the carrier accepts that the loss is covered but you disagree on how much it costs. Get the carrier’s full estimate and any letters explaining its position. Compare it with your contractor’s estimate so you know exactly where the numbers differ.","url":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/#step-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"Read the appraisal condition","text":"Find the Appraisal paragraph in the conditions section of your policy. Note who can demand appraisal, how the demand must be made, the time to name an appraiser (often 20 days) and how the umpire is chosen. Look for any endorsement that changes the standard wording.","url":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/#step-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Send a written demand","text":"Either side can usually invoke appraisal in writing. A clear demand identifies the claim, states that you disagree on the amount of loss, invokes the appraisal provision and names your appraiser or says you will within the policy deadline. Keep proof of delivery.","url":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/#step-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Each side names an appraiser","text":"You choose a competent and impartial appraiser, and so does the carrier. Each side pays its own. Your appraiser inspects the property, builds an independent estimate and gathers the photos and measurements to support it.","url":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/#step-4"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":5,"name":"The appraisers select an umpire","text":"The two appraisers try to agree on a neutral umpire, often within 15 days. If they cannot, either side may usually ask a court in the county where the property is located to appoint one. The umpire’s fee is normally split.","url":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/#step-5"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":6,"name":"The appraisers work the differences","text":"The appraisers compare estimates line by line. Most items are resolved here, sometimes on site. Anything they agree on is set; only disputed items move on.","url":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/#step-6"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":7,"name":"The umpire decides what is left","text":"The umpire reviews the remaining items, sometimes with an inspection and written submissions from each appraiser, then joins one appraiser or the other on each item.","url":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/#step-7"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":8,"name":"The award is signed and paid","text":"An award signed by any two of the three sets the amount of loss. The carrier then pays according to the policy: the award, less the deductible, prior payments and any depreciation not yet recoverable.","url":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/#step-8"}],"@id":"https://vermontinsuranceappraiser.com/vermont-appraisal-process/#howto"}]}</script>
